  "hints": [
    "Write a with the definition of odd, then substitute into a² + 3a + 5.",
    "After expanding, aim for the shape 2·(integer) + 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $a$ is odd, $a = 2k + 1$ for some integer $k$.",
    "$a^2 + 3a + 5 = (2k+1)^2 + 3(2k+1) + 5 = 4k^2 + 10k + 9 = 2(2k^2 + 5k + 4) + 1$.",
    "$2k^2 + 5k + 4$ is an integer, so $a^2 + 3a + 5$ is odd. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
